# Commands run by the launchd job com.redwood.demo (see userland/com.redwood.demo.plist) in the image the
# ios-safari-mcp server boots. Build with ./build-image.sh
# The default rc.jobs runs diagnostics (cpu_test 240 & burns CPU while SpringBoard starts) and never configures
# the network, so Safari says "not connected to the Internet". This is rc.jobs.net's DHCP step on QEMU's virtio en0
# (see userland/src/net_test.m) and a lookup. It needs the on-demand jobs (configd): see the RWA_PACKED16 fix in mkjobs.py.
/redwood/bin/net_test show dhcp en0 waitaddr en0 90
/redwood/bin/net_test resolve example.com reach example.com
